# IN-SCOPE: The working tree on claude/laughing-edison-x0pdv8 matches the patch byte for byte, and it touches only NOTES.md (12 lines added, 4 removed). The only change is in the v2.64.26 entry under "On staging, waiting on a device pass": the "What this costs" sentence is replaced and everything around it is unchanged. That is change 1 of the plan and nothing else. Every claim in the new text holds against the code. `PREVIEW_PIPELINE` is 66 now and was 65 at ed3870d^, where ed3870d moved it, and `previewKey` puts it first in the key, so every stored preview misses once and is rendered again. In the current code, `lensPlanFor` lays `lensStrengthAtOpen`, which is now 1 with a matched profile and 0 without one. `applySnapshot` restores the photograph's own `lensFix` (for an older edit with no `lensFix` stored, it keeps the open's value through the merge). On the next draw, `ensureLensApplied` calls `bringLensTo`, which makes one ratio pass only when the strength differs from what the decode laid. `makeThumb` calls `bringLensTo` only for an own edit, and each tile comes from a fresh decode in `oneThumbnail`. So one pass per open and one per tile, only for a matched raw whose own strength is not 1, is correct. For a raw with no matched lens, `lensCurveFor` returns null, so `lensPlanFor` returns null and `bringLensTo` resolves to strength 0 against an empty stamp, which matches what is already there, so no pass runs. At ed3870d^, `lensStrengthAtOpen` returned `rememberedStrength(key) ?? 1`, so the decode laid the remembered strength and the old inline `ensureLensApplied` skipped the pass when the photograph's strength equalled it. The old `makeThumb` had no re-apply at all: the tile's pixels carried the decode's strength and `lensForEdit` returned null for a linear source. A pass between two strengths of the same curve uses one gain table size, so it is a single pass, not two. Two small points leave the claims true because the text says "whenever" and not "only when": a bypassed lens also causes a pass, and a photograph at 1 with nothing remembered also skipped it before. The text states no measured time and says outright that the pass's time on a device was not measured. The only numbers it gives are the version numbers, 65 and 66. No one is quoted or named, and there is no table.
